# KASIM ELITE DIGITAL — ASSET GUIDE

Last corrected: 20 September 2026. Replaces every earlier version.

---

## 1. HOW THE PORTFOLIO USES IMAGES

Two layers, and they do different jobs.

**In the page:** hand-coded SVG mockups inside laptop, plate and phone
frames, animated on scroll — chart paths draw themselves, figures count
up. These are the proof that you build interfaces, not just pictures of
them. They are never replaced by a photo.

**Behind a button:** each device frame carries a **View concept**
control. It opens the full-resolution render over the page, with
previous/next paging through all ten. Nothing is covered; the visual
render is one tap away at a size where it reads.

The renders are AI-generated concept explorations. Every caption says
so. They support a capability claim — they do not prove delivery. Only
live projects do that.

---

## 2. WHAT EACH PAGE LOADS

| Page | Images it requests |
|------|--------------------|
| index.html | `logo.png`, `banner.jpg`, `profile.jpg` |
| portfolio.html | `logo.png` + the ten files in `/work` (lightbox only) |
| services.html | `logo.png` — 107 inline SVGs, no image slots |
| store.html | `logo.png` — 67 inline SVGs |
| about.html | `logo.png`, `profile.jpg`, `profile-full.jpg` |
| contact.html | `logo.png` |

Before adding an image anywhere, search the page for the filename. If
the HTML does not ask for it, uploading it changes nothing.

---

## 3. THE /work FOLDER — REQUIRED

```
/portfolio.html
/logo.png
/work
  case-01.jpg  Nexura — fintech design system        1600x1000
  case-02.jpg  CryptoAd — vertical ad creative       1200x825
  case-03.jpg  Aetheria — portfolio dashboard        1600x1000
  case-04.jpg  QuantumFlow — automation pipeline     1200x825
  case-05.jpg  Valoris — portfolio screen             540x1140
  case-05b.jpg Valoris — market pulse screen          540x1140
  case-06.jpg  GlobalShop — multilingual storefront  1200x825
  case-07.jpg  Neonex — motion identity board        1200x825
  case-08.jpg  BlockTrade — exchange dashboard       1600x1000
  case-09.jpg  kasimempire.com — studio site         1600x1000
```

All ten are required. Paths are relative to the repo root:
`work/case-01.jpg`. Flat folder, `.jpg`, zero-padded, lowercase.

Nothing loads until a visitor opens the viewer — the images are set
from JavaScript, and neighbours are preloaded on open. The page costs
nothing extra on first paint.

To replace one: keep the filename, match the pixel size above, export
JPEG quality ~84 progressive, under 250 KB.

---

## 4. UPLOADING TO GITHUB WITHOUT BREAKING THINGS

1. **Check the filename after download.** Windows appends ` (1)` when
   the name already exists in Downloads. `logo (1).png` will 404.
2. **Lowercase, hyphens, no spaces.** GitHub and Vercel are
   case-sensitive; Windows is not. `Logo.PNG` works on the laptop and
   fails in production.
3. **Edit HTML in place** — pencil icon, select all, paste, commit.
   Never delete and re-add a file; that loses history and briefly 404s
   the page.
4. **Verify on the live URL**, not locally. Hard refresh or use a
   private tab.

---

## 5. WHY A MISSING IMAGE IS INVISIBLE

The page itself looks perfect whether or not `/work` exists — the
coded mockups carry it. A missing render only shows when someone opens
the viewer, where it appears as an empty frame.

**So the portfolio looking right is not proof the images uploaded.**
After any push, open one card's viewer and page through all ten with
the arrow keys.

---

## 6. BRAND TOKENS

```css
--bg-primary:#050505;  --bg-secondary:#0a0a0a;
--gold-primary:#D4AF37; --gold-light:#FFDF00; --gold-deep:#B8860B;
--royal-blue:#1E3A8A;  --accent-blue:#3B82F6;
--text-main:#FFFFFF;   --text-muted:#9CA3AF;
```

Display type: Cormorant Garamond. Body and UI: Inter.

Logo and founder portraits are used as supplied — never recoloured,
redrawn, or cropped past the framing already agreed.
